# Manifest for tests/uae/run_real_exe_test.sh - see that script's own
# header for the format. hexagon2.exe is a real Amiga program (not one
# of gen_corpus.py's synthetic items) that already prints a fixed
# string over the serial port on startup ("Hello debugger from
# Amiga!") with no extra instrumentation needed - unlike hexagon.exe,
# it doesn't loop printing a heartbeat afterward, so HEARTBEAT_CHECK
# is left at its default (0): SENTINEL alone is the whole pass
# condition.
#
# Added to the tracked real-exe suite after this exact file caught a
# real bug: a 68000 Address Error in RelocFixup's reloc-stream escape
# handling (see the commit that added this .meta), reproducible only
# on a real (large, relocation-heavy) program - execram's synthetic
# corpus never triggered it. Keeping this file exercised here going
# forward is a regression guard against exactly that class of bug.
SENTINEL="Hello debugger from Amiga!"
